{:title
 "Lens in the Smile Prompt Language, Many Ways of Looking Over One Pool of Prompts",
 :description
 "What a lens is in THE MAP of Smile, a way of looking that places every piece at a position with its name, dressing and defaults, many lenses over one pool, formats as lenses and the lens as a fork of token alternatives, and how my words reached it, from a 2023 request to label each word with attention, through the Smile Token Lens of July 2026, to ontologies named lenses in August 2026, with every source.",
 :keywords
 "prompt ontology, lens, prompt library organisation, logprobs viewer, token lens, formats as lenses, Smile prompt language, history of Smile",
 :lede
 "In THE MAP, a lens says how things appear when looked through. Many lenses look over one pool, all real, each one a way of looking.",
 :paras
 ["THE MAP keeps the compositions and each thing's shared card in the pool, and a lens keeps placements, this piece is here, called this, wearing this, meaning this. One piece, many lenses, one copy, and moving a thing inside a lens reclassifies it. Everything is placed at a position along a route such as Main/Prompt Instruction/Avoid Words, and defaults resolve down the route, so the deepest position sets what a piece wears. Anyone makes their own lens and uses parts of others, and crossover points where two lenses place one thing differently are links between them. A person has an ontology and an AI has its own, and the relationship between them is a lens of its own. A format, such as prompts or transcripts, is a lens over its kind. And the lens is also a fork, every token position it shows being a place a generation could have gone another way."
 "Before Smile, in October 2023, I asked a model to show its attention word by word, “for each word in your last response, label with [attention amount] using scale described prior”.[[m:2023-10-14]] In October 2025 the planned GUI was to show the logprobs of each word, “You can preview the logprobs of each word and see the most likely and least likely words”.[[m:2025-10-29]]"
 "In July 2026 the Smile Token Lens was built, a view of a local model's tokens. On 22 July I asked for “a companion interface that runs simultaneous (or post if need be) when i do an LMStudio prompt”.[[m:2026-07-22#2]] On 23 July, “every time I send a message on my llama-ui (which is all logged currently) I get to see all of the logprobs at each token”, and “rename the project from Mikupad to Smile Token Lens”.[[m:2026-07-23]] On 25 July, “lets make it Smile Lens also.”[[m:2026-07-25]]"
 "In August 2026 the ontology of prompts became the lens. On 31 July, “ohhh we've needed to integrate the ontology into this the whole time”.[[m:2026-07-31]] On 1 August, “write in a massive ontological thing like Main body/Prompt Instruction/Avoid words and then for all the folders to exist”.[[m:2026-08-01]] On 4 August, “Ontologies - multiple ontologies viewed onto the prompt space, people make their own ontologies”, and “what if you could click through at crossover points between your ontology and others.”[[m:2026-08-04]] On 5 August, “anyone CAN make their own ontology, and use parts of ours.”[[m:2026-08-05]] On 6 August, “we definitely already have two ontologies, my personal ontology and the default smile ontology”.[[m:2026-08-06]] On 8 August came the name, “i found my first name claude, lets call an ontology lens, or lenses”.[[m:2026-08-08]] On 15 August, “a lens defines the point at which something is perceiving”, and “you could make a lens for xml and for markdown that things could be parsed into”.[[m:2026-08-15]]"
 "From late August the lens reached other documents and formats. On 2 September, “these archetpyal forms or templates are just lenses that let you see the commonality between documents of their format”.[[m:2026-09-02]] On 4 September, “Every time we decompose a text file, we integrate it into every lens using AI.”[[m:2026-09-04]] On 12 September the token lens returned as the fork, “we also need to be able to generate automatically from the variant tokens, e.g. a low probability token”.[[m:2026-09-12]] On 11 October, “The human and the AI each have their own ontology, and the relationship entity between them that is their interactions and co creation creating friction agency is its own entity”.[[m:2026-10-11]] On 16 October in OSRSangha, “the prompt catgegores are purely based on function, what they actually do in that interaction”.[[m:2026-10-16]]"
 "So the lens moved from attention labelled word by word in 2023, through a token viewer for a local model, to the ontologies anyone is to make over one pool, the formats, and the relationship between a person and an AI, across {{moments}} moments and {{quotes}} quotes from {{first}} to {{last}}. The depth a lens is viewed at is followed in [[t:magnification]]."],
 :faq
 [["What is a lens in Smile?"
 "A way of looking over one pool of prompts. A lens places each piece at a position, with its name, dressing and defaults, and anyone can make their own lens and use parts of others. Making your own lens is still to be built."]
 ["Why is an ontology called a lens in Smile?"
 "A lens defines the point from which something is perceived. On 8 August 2026 I named ontologies lenses, and many can look over the same pool at once."]
 ["What is the token lens?"
 "A lens built in July 2026, which shows a local model's log probabilities at each token. It became the fork, where any alternative token can be taken and the reply regenerated from it."]]}
